When the user types **"start"** (or any equivalent like "porneste", "pornește bucla", "resume loop", "start monitor") while the working directory is the `{{PROJECT_NAME}}` repo, do all of the following in order, **without asking further questions** (the setup is already approved at `init` time):

## 1. Re-arm the {{PROVIDER}} Monitor

The polling script and env file already exist under `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`:

- Script: `<MEM>/monitor.sh`
- Env: `<MEM>/.env` (chmod 600)
- State file: `<MEM>/.monitor-state` — **delete it before re-arming** so the first tick re-emits the current queue.

Steps:

1. `rm -f <MEM>/.monitor-state <MEM>/.pr-monitor-state`
2. Call the **Monitor** tool with:
   - `command`: `<MEM>/monitor.sh`
   - `description`: `{{PROJECT_NAME}} {{READY_STATUS}} queue (new/changed actionable issues)`
   - `persistent`: `true`
   - `timeout_ms`: `3600000`
3. Call **Monitor** again for the PR watcher:
   - `command`: `<MEM>/monitor-prs.sh`
   - `description`: `{{PROJECT_NAME}} loop-owned PRs (merge/close/comments/CI)`
   - `persistent`: `true`
   - `timeout_ms`: `3600000`

   The loop is an **independent instrument** — it sees merges/comments/CI by itself and self-triggers the next task; the owner communicates ONLY via PR + tracker comments, never chat pings.
4. Note both returned `task_id`s; they are the wake signals for the loop.

If an old Monitor for the same script is still running, `TaskStop` it first.

## 2. Verify the {{PROVIDER}} queue once

Run one curl against `{{PROVIDER}}`'s API to check whether anything is already in `{{READY_STATUS}}` — the Monitor needs ~60s for its first tick. Use the "Verify queue" recipe from the provider doc. Do **not** include backlog items (per [[feedback-only-ready-not-backlog]]).

If issues are returned, **triage the queue first** — mark every ready ticket with the `LOOP-PLAN` vocabulary (order / group / depends-on), autonomously per [[feedback-queue-triage-plan]] — then **start processing per the plan immediately** following the spec in [[autonomous-loop]]. If empty, just confirm "Monitor pornit, coadă goală, aștept evenimente" (or English equivalent) and continue to step 3.

## 3. Arm the dynamic /loop safety net

Call **ScheduleWakeup** with:

- `delaySeconds`: `1500` (25 min fallback heartbeat; Monitor is the primary wake signal)
- `reason`: short one-liner like `"Monitor primary wake; 25-min safety heartbeat"`
- `prompt` (verbatim, exactly this string — prefix with `/loop `):

  ```
  /loop Run one iteration of the autonomous {{PROJECT_NAME}} task loop as specified in memory file autonomous-loop.md: FIRST sweep the loop's own PRs — address new review comments (viewing attached images/videos, ffmpeg frames for video), fix red CI (a regression is a hard blocker), merge approved PRs with green CI yourself, and move merged PRs' {{PROVIDER}} issues to Merged/closest completed state — then, if fewer than 3 loop-owned PRs are open, check the {{READY_STATUS}} queue: when its content changed, autonomously re-triage it and mark every ready ticket with the LOOP-PLAN vocabulary (order / group / depends-on) without asking, then pull the next issue per the plan (parallel groups as worktree agents up to the WIP headroom; PRs awaiting review never pause the queue — only an unmerged depends-on or a full WIP cap does), read its full context including media, identify the target service subdirectory, branch from fresh origin/main, implement using the repo's matching skills with the diff scoped strictly to the task, ship tests with the change, verify with Playwright MCP, run the full local test suite, scan the diff for secrets, push, open a GitHub PR fully autonomously with no AI attribution and mandatory before/after (and design-vs-implementation) evidence for UI changes, watch CI, run /review plus the rigorous critique plus the security pass plus the QA-agent gate, and only when all gates are green move the {{PROVIDER}} issue to {{REVIEW_STATUS}} and post the PR URL. Mirror any TODO the diff introduces as a backlog task. Timebox stuck tasks: after ~3 failed attempts document the blocker on the issue, hand it back, move on. Re-read MEMORY.md every tick and apply every feedback rule. Self-pace: if no open task is available, sleep ~1200s before checking again.
  ```

## 4. Pre-flight checks before "go"

Re-read `MEMORY.md` first to refresh every feedback rule (no AI attribution, autonomous LOOP-PLAN triage of the ready queue on every change, run tests locally, ship tests WITH every behavior change, regression on PR checks = hard blocker, security pass + secrets scan on every PR, diff scoped strictly to the task, vetted dependencies only, screenshots in PR branch for private repos, mandatory before/after + design-vs-implementation evidence, pull main each task — default branch only via PR, run `/review` + `rigorous` critique + the QA agent gate on every PR, watch the loop's open PRs for feedback before new tasks, actually view comment media — ffmpeg frames for videos, merge approved PRs yourself, move merged PRs' tickets to Merged/Done, WIP cap of 3 open PRs, timebox stuck tasks after ~3 attempts, use project skills, TODO → backlog task, persist new corrections, only ready not backlog, etc.).

## Background context (do not re-prompt the user)

- Loop spec: see [[autonomous-loop]].
- The user has explicitly authorized fully autonomous PR creation (no confirmation gate).
- If the user says "stop" / "opreste" / "kill loop", call `TaskStop` on the Monitor task id and DO NOT call `ScheduleWakeup`.
